 hydrogen:['H','Hydrogen nuclei','primordial','Most ordinary-matter mass remains in hydrogen.','Roughly 75% hydrogen and 25% helium by primordial baryonic mass, excluding dark matter and dark energy.'],
 helium:['He','Helium','primordial + stellar','Helium-4 nuclei form early; stars add more later.','Helium becomes neutral earlier than hydrogen. Chapter boundaries simplify extended processes.'],
 lithium:['Li','Trace light isotopes','primordial traces','Deuterium, helium-3 and lithium-7 accompany H/He.','Much primordial lithium-7 comes through beryllium-7 decay. Its predicted abundance disagrees with old-star measurements.'],
 atoms:['H / He','Hydrogen & helium gas','gas','Atoms form as plasma cools; starlight later ionizes much gas again.','Matter cycles between ions, atoms, molecules and stars. Atoms are not permanent once formed.'],
 cmb:['γ','Microwave background','relic radiation','Pre-existing thermal photons redshift after last scattering; recombination does not create the entire CMB.','Today its temperature is about 2.7255 K. Late-time temperatures here refer to this radiation, not all gas.'],
