 iron:['Fe','Iron-group elements','stellar explosions','Explosions, including Type Ia supernovae, supply iron-group nuclei.','Nickel-56 decays through cobalt-56 to iron-56. Not every star makes iron.'],
 heavy:['Au','Neutron-capture elements','multiple sources','Slow capture in evolved stars and rapid capture in neutron-rich events build heavy nuclei.','Neutron-star mergers are an observed r-process site. Exact fractions vary by isotope; additional pathways exist.'],
 dust:['Si C','Dust, rock & metal','condensed matter','Enriched environments allow solid grains to condense.','Grains grow in gas and can be destroyed by shocks. Solids and ices help build planets.'],
